   {
    "id": "q1",
    "text": "What is the register map (offset, width, reset value and access of every register) of the shell-facing block?",
    "default": "The map in registers.map: ID 0x00 RO, ACT_LO/HI 0x04/0x08, WGT_LO/HI 0x0C/0x10, BIAS 0x14, MULT_SHIFT 0x18, CTRL 0x1C (go), STATUS 0x20, Y 0x24, ACC 0x28; 32-bit words, reset 0 except ID.",
    "reason": "The request names the shell and loading but gives no offsets, so the map is a proposal.",
    "answer": "A_LO: offset 0x00, RW, reset 0: [31:0] activations 0..3, a_i in bits [8i+7:8i]\nA_HI: offset 0x01, RW, reset 0: [31:0] activations 4..7, a_(4+i) in bits [8i+7:8i]\nW_LO: offset 0x02, RW, reset 0: [31:0] weights 0..3, same packing\nW_HI: offset 0x03, RW, reset 0: [31:0] weights 4..7, same packing\nBIAS: offset 0x04, RW, reset 0: [31:0] signed bias\nMULT: offset 0x05, RW, reset 0: [15:0] unsigned multiplier; [31:16] read 0\nCTRL: offset 0x06, RW, reset 1: [4:0] shift (1..31), [8] relu; other bits read 0\nGO: offset 0x07, WO, reset 0: any write starts one computation; reads 0\nY: offset 0x08, RO, reset 0: [7:0] limited answer (two's complement); [31:8] read 0\nACC: offset 0x09, RO, reset 0: [31:0] the signed accumulator including the bias\nSTATUS: offset 0x0A, RO, reset 0: [0] READY; other bits 0\nshell: shell/PROTOCOL.md (version 1.0)\nunmapped: offsets 0x0B-0x7F read 0; writes to them and to RO registers are ignored",
