   {
    "id": "q2",
    "text": "Is acc allowed to overflow 32 bits when bias is near its limit?",
    "default": "Wrap in 32 bits; the reported acc and the scaling both use the wrapped value.",
    "reason": "The request calls acc signed 32-bit and gives no saturation rule.",
    "answer": "The specification does not allow overflow: it says the sum never overflows for the allowed inputs. It does not define whether a bias near its limit counts as an allowed input, and it does not specify any wrap behaviour, so the proposed 32-bit wrap default is not supported by the spec.",
    "status": "answered",
    "by": "oracle",
    "evidence": "acc = sum over i<8 of a_i * w_i + bias (signed arithmetic; a_i and w_i signed 8-bit, bias signed 32-bit; the sum never overflows for the allowed inputs)"
