   {
    "id": "q3",
    "text": "Is ready cleared when a new go is accepted, and are results held until then?",
    "default": "Yes, ready drops on go and rises when the new y and acc are valid; results held otherwise.",
    "reason": "The request only says ready indicates a result, not what happens on a second go.",
    "answer": "Yes. A write to GO clears READY and presents the operands for one clock; READY becomes 1 within 8 clocks and stays 1 until the next GO; Y and ACC hold the result until the next GO and read 0 while READY is 0.",
